From d3fe06b1ebc76c0f3673957069fab17251e90352 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barisyild <25794892+barisyild@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 05:24:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Make blockElement iterative instead of recursing per
 statement
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`blockElement` walked a block's statement list by recursing once per element,
so a block of N statements cost N eval-stack frames. Compiling a large
generated program — 87,000 lines of machine-written Haxe — exhausted the stack
and failed with "Uncaught exception Stack overflow", with no indication of
which construct was responsible.

Every recursive call was already in tail position: the frames carried nothing
the next iteration could not read from `acc` and `el`. So the recursion is a
loop, and the transformation is mechanical — each `return blockElement(a, b)`
becomes `acc = a; el = b; continue;` inside a `while(true)`.

The one non-tail call, a `switch` on the else-branch of a constant `if`, is
rewritten as an explicit if/else assigning `el` before continuing.

With this, a program that previously overflowed compiles in 63 seconds.
